DUHHHHH...damn windows!!

My problem was that althugh i enabled dhcp on my windows client from teh
network card, I had disabled the DHCP client from within the services
panel!!!! I had forgotten about doing this and since windows is not smart
enough to complain teh the dchp service is not available it took my a
little while to track down the problem....

Just thought i'd pass this on to anyone who might have no idea why dhcp
server might not work on their network ;)...

John





