	Am (still) trying to get Redhat 7.2 running on a DEC ALPHA 2100 =
(A500MP) machine.  Am now using an ADPTEC 1742A (EISA slot 3)as the SCSI =
controller for the hard disks.  I boot from the installed CDROM drive, =
attached to a NCR53C810 (EISA slot1), using the command 'b dka6 -fl 3' =
for text based installation.   The installation procedure runs through =
to completion with no errors.   Trouble is I can not boot from the hard =
disk(s) after completing the install.

	During the installation I select the autopartioning function and the =
following mount points are assigned:
	/dev/sda1	/boot
	/dev/sdb1	/
	/dev/sdc1	/var
	/dev/sdd1	/home
	/dev/sde1	/usr
	/dev/sdf1	swap

Note:   Each scsi disk is a separate physical unit (2.1 gig ea)

	After installation is complete, perform a reboot (power down) and enter =
the following at the SRM prompt:     b dkb1 -fi vmlinuz -fl =
root=3D/dev/sdb1

	The hard disk (sda) access light illuminate and Linux starts to load =
and then fails with the following messages:  =20

	cannot open root device on sdb1 or 08:21,   please append a correct =
'root' boot option.   	kernel panic:   VFS:   unable to mount root file =
system on 08:21.

If any body can provide some pointers as to where I am going wrong or =
what I have done wrong, it would be greatly appreciated.

thanx

Craig ryder
		=09

=09




