On Tue, Mar 04, 2003 at 12:32:49AM -0000, Simon Tierney wrote:
>
> I have now tried HP technical support and they are saying the SROMs of the
> 7305 CPUs are coded for NT only.

The FLASH of the 7305 has both NT and SRM consoles, BUT...

...the SRM console will NOT run Tru64, BUT...

...it WILL run Linux... :-)

The 7305 was never sold "Linux-ready" (as some other machines were)
but ONLY for running NT, hence the answers by Support.

> Debian does list it as unsupported, but as RedHat 7.2 boots successfully,
> and only fails to detect drives available to install on, this suggests to me
> the DAC960 is the problem.

Correct; the latest DAC960 Linux driver wants firmware 2.73 or later,
and many of the older DAC960s sold by DEC, in such boxes as the 7305,
have DEC custom firmware 2.70 or older.

> http://www.mylex.com/products/index.html
> 
> lists fwpd273.exe as the upgrade for single prom -is this appropriate?

Yes, but ONLY for non-DEC DAC960s...

WARNING!!!

I don't believe it is wise to try to use the Mylex firmware with the
DEC utility, or the Mylex utility with the DEC firmware - you are just
asking for trouble.

But DEC firmware (2.70) that WILL work with a (patched) DAC960 Linux
driver can be downloaded, with utility and docs, from an HP site.

See the attached previous posting that has the URL and much additional
information.

Good luck.

 --Jay++

