On Tue, Mar 04, 2003 at 09:55:55PM -0000, Simon Tierney wrote:
> 
> I think I understand.   I tried to update the DAC960 firmware to 2.73 on the
> basis that RedHat 7.2 might then recognise it.

RH 7.2 would recognize it, I believe, and allow straightforward
install.  Newer DAC960s with newer firmware (3.xx or 4.xx) are
recognized and can be installed to.

> There is a page that offers this upgrade for the DAC960PU:-
> http://www.mylex.com/support/productgd/index.html

I believe the Mylex executable is x86 only, so you'd have to put the
DAC960 into an INTEL box to do the FLASHing.

Of course, that's assuming that the Mylex FLASH utility would work
with the OEM'ed card, ie that the hardware is identical. I believe
this to be the case, that only the firmware is actually different, but
I don't know if this is true. Perhaps you might get someone at Mylex
to comment.

> Is it a one way function, or can I reflash back to 2.7 if it doesn't work?

Sorry, but I don't know the answer to that question.

 --Jay++

