Hello again,

I just disconnected the DAC960 and installed a PCI SCSI controller with a
disk connected  by the ribbon externally using an extension to the auxiliary
power source in the expansion slot at the front.

You can't fit the ribbon through the aperture in the case!

The idea was to install to the scsi drive and recompile a patched kernel
that can operate the DAC960.

Now the PCI SCSI card and drive are recognised but the CD-ROM device has
become invalid.   Aargh!

I took the time to read through the dandelion.com DAC960 site last night but
the drivers require 2.73 firmware, so it doesn't look like they'll help me.

I have another Linux system, but it's intel.   Can I compile a patched
kernel on that, or will it pick up wrong information during configure / make
stages?

Do I need a different source tarball?

Sorry if I'm asking stupid questions, but I haven't come accross a problem
like this before.

Simon

