    Don't waste your money. Search the archives and you'll see
    plenty of us telling others that it's not worth the hassle.

    To "upgrade" a CPU, you have to upgrade cache and
    possibly SROM code too. With that said, even if you
    got all the parts, you still need lab-quality equipment to
    desolder and re-solder the components and CPU. Sockets
    probably won't work due to signalling issues. There were
    some used in lab environments, but rarely, if ever, would
    you find it in a production board.

    RE: Slot-B  Ugh, don't even TRY resoldering a CPU onto
    this board. It's something like a 12 layer board and one
    wrong move and you've got a paperweight.

    Buy the CPU for a paperweight.


mike


