On Tue, Mar 11, 2003 at 01:01:18PM -0600, Hoover, Tony wrote:
> 
> Has RHN dropped support for Alpha?  I know that support for 7.2 comes direct
> from HP, But I thought that 7.1 and prior were still supported through RHN.

A fragment of announcement dated "19 Dec 2002" and with a title
"Errata policy updates and product end of life".

<quote>
In addition, the
following products have now reached their end of life for errata and are
no longer supported:

      Red Hat Linux PowerTools (6.2, 7, and 7.1)
      All Red Hat Linux releases for the Alpha and Sparc architectures
      Red Hat Linux 7.1 for the IA64 architecture

This policy, as well as our current errata and advisories, are available
from http://www.redhat.com/apps/support/errata/
</quote>

Actually most of the updates from HPC for 7.2, and maybe even all,
will fit just fine your 7.1 installation if you do not feel like
recompiling things yourself.  Across 7.x releases libraries are
compatible.  Only when a major version changes you can expect
that ABI is different as well.  Still 'rpmbuild --rebuild ....src.rpm'
is very often all what you need.

  Michal




