rm.riches@verizon.net wrote:
> On Feb. 21, my UP2000 motherboard died.  It was my only machine,
> so I went and bought a "temporary" X86 setup and installed RH8.0
> on it.  It's a Pentium 4 "A" with 512KB cache at 1.8GHz.  [...]
> 
> The surprise to me was that this thing is actually much faster on
> all of my java code than the Alpha.  The Alpha machine in
> question was/is a 667MHz EV67 (one CPU) on a UP2000 mobo [...]

Oh well, you are comparing a EV67 CPU and MOBO/chipset (which
hit the market back in '99, and which came late, IIRC) with a
PIV "Northwood" CPU and chipset combination from '02 and you
are still expecting a fair result from your comparision? Using
non-native code, beeing mainly dependent on "middleware", that
has "questionable" support for Alphas since at least 1999)?

Alpha is dead. Since Compaq declared it to be dead back in '99.
Period. It's sad, but it's the truth.


Stefan Schroepfer




