Seems to me that HP just released Marvel, based on the EV7 chipset.
And...oh my, but haven't I also heard something about EV79. And...if
Itanium II is late..would we see EV8? Probably not but I've been accused of
being overly optimistic in the past. Alpha isn't dead. Perhaps in two or
three or four years we will all look around at how much progress has been
made in the sciences, consider how our lives have been enriched by it, and
it just may occur to some that "Wow..Alpha wasn't dead in 2001, 2002, or
2003" as so many claim.

cheers
~m

