I would have to agree with your mention of cost for Alpha. Like PA-RISC,
SPARC and and Power 4, there is a great deal that goes into the
architecture, and it's not just about the chip. But compare the systems,
and you can go back as far as 1992 when Alpha was introduced and find the
clear leader has been Alpha. 

I just feel it's a shame that other technologies (all be it inferior),
because they were introduced and driven by companies where one expect to
pay a premium for the RAS features structured around Alpha have been far
less the subject of this sort of hype.

So...you want to pay less on the front end for something far less robust
that will end up with more hidden cost....excuse me..I think I hear Intel
knocking at the door.

cheers
~m

