To the list:

I've got no problem with the dork side at all  ... except it won't run 
ArcInfo for Digital Unix.  As long as I have access to a valid ArcInfo 
license, there will be an Alpha workstation in my life.  Oh, yeah, they run 
ArcInfo like blazes.

I-86, well you never know how good the stuff is until you run it under Linux. 
 When I was using windows, I thought the x86 architecture was crap.  But 
under Linux, well it's another matter.  Put a nice, red hat on her, and you 
wouldn't recognize the old wh..,er, chip.

The other reason for having an Alpha machine around is I can't afford a 
Maserati or a Vincent Black Shadow and anyway they are kinda greasy and you 
have to crawl under them.  The Alpha satisfies those kinds of cravings for 
me. 

On the Tru64 list the other day there was a guy asking about books he could 
read to bone up on AIX.  His shop had taken a look at the situation and 
decided that if they had to change architectures and OS at the same time, 
they might as well go with Big Blue.  I think a lot of HPQ customers may be 
thinking that way.

jn

"Thursday"




