>performance gain over the existing Itanium II may be as equally great.

This seemed to be the main problem with the Alpha processor; its price
seemed in general to be an order of magnitude higher than the typical
P4 processor, but its performance did not match that level of pricing.
It was very difficult to justify purchasing an Alpha server when a P4
server was able to at least keep up with, and many times surpassing,
the Alpha at less than half the price, regardless of architectural
advantages.

Based on the SPEC benchmarks that I've seen for the Itanium, it has the
same price/performance disadvantage.

