	Thanx to every one for the assistance, problem was the 'aha1740' module not being included in 'initrd'.   To fix the problem, booted into "rescue" mode from the CD and edited /etc/modules.conf to include an additional "alias scsi_hostadapter aha1740" line.    Did not have to include any IRQs etc.   Executed "mkinitrd" to create a new ram disk image.   Power cycled the system and the machine booted fine.

	An interesting quirk of RH 7.2 I discovered today, when performing an "update packages" from CD.   All non-comment lines in the 'aboot.conf' file get erased.   Bit of a trap so beware.

rgds

Craig Ryder



