Oh...one other thing I just remembered...some of the DPT Ultra160 
RAID cards were actually recalled because of a buggy Qlogic 
chip.  If the card is recognized, but the drives aren't 
functioning right, yours might be one such card.  I don't know 
what the exact details of the bug were, just that it was 
critical enough to issue a recall.

If your card was part of the recall, you might be able to get 
Adaptec to do an exchange.  It's been ages since the recall, but 
Adaptec (unlike QLogic) is pretty good about taking 
responsibility for defective parts.

-- 
Kelledin
