Hi Folks,

I installed RH 7.2 onto my UP2000+ boxes a few months ago because it
was the latest and greatest.  However, I soon found that a lot of the
apps I built under it ran much slower than before.  Tracing the problem
down to the lowest level, I found the core to be in our software using
FFTW.  At first I thought it was because we rebuilt it using GCC
3.0.4.  I had kept a set of FFTW test programs built with GCC 2.96 under
RH 7.1, so I ran it to compare against the new versions that were built
with GCC 3.0.4 as well as 2.96, both under RH 7.2.  What I found was a
big descrpency in performance.  The old programs, run under the new OS,
would be consistently faster than the new programs by nearly 40%.  Now,
this is an extreme case, because I think my applications have slowed
down by "only" 20% when built under the new OS.

Are there any different compile flags I need to use to get back the
performance?  I'm going to back one of my systems down to RH 7.1 just
to verify this.

thanks,
eyc





