Seems unlikely. I guess either the old version was compiled with
CPU-specific flags, or you're using a different libm. Try recompiling
with a recent gcc and -mcpu=ev67.

You might also want to try the Super Page patch
(http://shimizu-lab.dt.u-tokai.ac.jp/lsp.html), it sometimes helps for
programs with large working set.

