On Mon, Mar 24, 2003 at 03:30:38PM -0800, Eugene Chu wrote:
> 
> Another thing, after I did make xconfig for my kernel, I find that the
> Makefile did not recognize make bzImage.

'bzImage' is an x86 specific target.  Use an architecture independent
'make boot'.

> I can make vmlinux and bzip2 the image myself, but is this normal?

'bzImage' has nothing to do with bzip2.  It is "big zImage" required by
some "features" of x86 architecture.  If you will use bzip2 on kernel
images you will have troubles to boot results. :-)

  Michal




