Some have mentioned on this list that they would like their alpha
running RedHat 7.2 to have an updated GUI.  I've also wanted the desktop
on my alpha looking the same as my x86 laptop running Redhat 8.0.  I
decided to take all source kde RPMs from Redhat 8.0 and compile them for
my alpha. I based the compilation on the standard 7.2 gcc toolchain
until the gcc 3.x bugs for the alpha get resolved and incorporated.

I was able to compile most of the kde RPMS without modification by
using the right path for versions of autoconf/automake.  I was not
able to get pilot-link, kdepim, kdeedu, kdebindings, or koffice to
compile because of autoconf, libtool, or other packaging errors.
I could fix the problems, but I have decided to hold off for the
upcoming kde 3.1 RPMs from RedHat 9.

I put the ~250 RPMs for kde3.0, XFree 4.2, cups, and related dependencies at
http://www.isi.edu/~lindell/alpha/RPMS/redhat-8.0/.

I tried running kde3 on my alpha using these RPMs and it seems to
run fine.  Other brave souls are welcome to try them out.

Bob




