After a bit of checking, I think I found the source of what I preceived
as the performance difference.  The confusion seems to be from the way
time is being obtained by the fftw_test program.  I noticed that even
though the old and new versions of the program report vastly different
results, they were both taking exactly the same CPU and clock times.
Unless the two programs, built from the same source code with the same
compiler, but under different versions of the OS, are actually running
different numbers of iterations for each FFT mode, their performance
are nearly identical.

This raises some questions:

Why are they reporting different times?
I'm guessing the sytem routines they're using must be reporting times
differently.

What IS the actual performance of FFTW on an Alpha EV67?
I ran my own tests using DXML and a simple FORTRAN FFT function, and
I get a set of numbers, but they are consistent between different
versions of OS.

My previous timings will have to be scrutinized, and fixed...

thanks for everyone's assistance.

eyc

PS:  I did manage to build a kernel customized for my processor (DP264),
and it had no significant affect on performance.  However, when I tried
to halt the system, the kernel panic'd and hung up.  No idea why.




