    The Linux kernel is dependant on GCC. You can't compile it with
    CCC.

    CCC is great for apps that really take advantage of the Alpha
    architecture. (floating point, etc...)

    Frankly, unless your app NEEDS CCC to really go fast, it's
    not worth the effort (debug/support/etc..)  to compile anything
    else with CCC for a minimal speed increase.
                                                                      mike

