The installer (fdisk) has always had problems with DOS labeled disks.  Please 
boot the install CD into rescue mode, run fdisk, type 'b' to create a bsd 
label, then 'w' to write it, then exit and reboot the CDs as you did before.  
This should fix the problem that you are seeing. 

We do have a specally patched version of fdisk that handles this issue 
correctly that will be on the new ISO images that are planned for release 
later in April.   The new images will  have all the updates produced during 
the past year and a 2.4.18-27.7.x.hp kernel (which is being tested).  If you 
have already applied all the current updates and upgrade to the new kernel 
(when it is ready), then you will not need the new ISO images.

I hope this helps.

Best Regards,


--George

P.S. - Please do not ask for more specific dates, as it depends completely 
upon the number of issues found during testing and the amount of time 
required to correct these problems, then more time to do retesting to be 
certain that no new problems were introduced and that the issue was actually 
resolved.

