Hi,
Thank you for the message Helge.

I have now installed RedHat 7.2 (with error message about anaconda) to a
drive attached to the NCR 53c810 bus, several times.

I get messages saying that there is a bad medium, but the files install on
retry.  Installation fails with an anaconda bug.

Thought at first the kernel couldn't mount the root filesystem because I had
declared ext3 instaed of ext2, but I got the same problemafter reformatting
& installing.

I have declared "-flags root=/dev/sda*" but I get the same message.
I have declared this as a flag in aboot after b /boot/vmlinuz but also as
the SRM variable -same result.

Can anyone explain what is going on?

Also, show * | more reveals that SRM has been arbitrarily adding CDs to the
variables and there are now 64 -how do I get rid of these, NVRAM is starting
to report itself full!

Any help would be appreciated as this is turning into quite a learning curve
for me!

Simon




